$DIR/main.p:5:25: cannot convert 3 (untyped int constant) to owner type sys.Fd outside package sys
    An owner owns memory or another resource and releases it when it is dropped,
    so it moves instead of being copied. Converting a plain untyped int into a
    sys.Fd would make a second owner of whatever the value refers to (a
    descriptor, a page frame), and both would release it. Only the package that
    declares sys.Fd may do that, where its invariants are kept.
    Use a constructor from the package that declares sys.Fd.
    (see "Conversions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.24)
    (run "pluto explain E3212" for a longer explanation)
